<Base title="About" active="about">
  <div class="page-prose">
    <h1>About GreenGrid India</h1>
    <p>
      <strong>GreenGrid India</strong> is an independent online publication covering India&rsquo;s
      renewable energy transition. We launched in <strong>July 2026</strong> and publish a new
      article every Sunday.
    </p>
    <p>
      India is in the middle of one of the world&rsquo;s largest clean energy build-outs &mdash;
      record solar and wind additions, a fast-growing storage market, a domestic manufacturing
      push, and an ambitious green hydrogen mission. Our goal is to make that story easy to follow:
      short, factual, well-sourced articles on the developments that matter.
    </p>

    <h2>What we cover</h2>
    <p>
      Solar (utility-scale and rooftop), wind, energy storage, green hydrogen, clean energy
      manufacturing, and the policy and market landscape — tenders, auctions, budgets and
      regulation.
    </p>

    <h2>Our approach</h2>
    <p>
      Every article lists the sources it draws on, including official releases from the Ministry of
      New and Renewable Energy (MNRE), SECI, industry research and reporting by established trade
      publications. We are a young publication and we&rsquo;d rather be accurate than first. If you
      spot an error, please tell us and we&rsquo;ll correct it promptly.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Editorial queries, tips and corrections: reach us at
      <a href="mailto:sambhavj.10@gmail.com">sambhavj.10@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Follow along</h2>
    <p>
      New articles are published every Sunday. Subscribe to our <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a> to
      never miss one.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
